{
  "rationale": "Use a small sensor plant plus a motion-capability plant, then a single deterministic policy specification that maps sensed obstacle conditions to exactly one safe action per state. The specification uses one-shot action states so open-loop motion pulses are issued conservatively, obstacle states never allow forward/random motion, path_clear returns quickly to exploration, and random_walk is the default clear-state exploration action with short move_forward used only in a dedicated progress state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate sensing and actuation into plant automata and encode the exploration policy in a compact deterministic specification",
    "Use clear/search and forward-progress helper states, with dedicated obstacle-recovery states that allow exactly one turn action and only return to exploration after path_clear"
  ],
